tasks.description:
Edit docs/how-it-works.md only, and add no tests that read the docs.

**Step 3, "Tempo and phase" (about line 180).** Describe:
- that once the winning grid is chosen, its 2/3, 3/4, 4/3 and 3/2 neighbours are scored against the low end (the kick), and the tracker moves to one only when the kick clearly supports it better;
- that half and double are still settled by the all-onset score and the 120 BPM preference, so a kick on every other beat gives the full tempo;
- the roughly 8-second hold (the length of the onset window) before following a tempo related to the locked one, where "related" means within 2% of 1/2, 2/3, 3/4, 4/3, 3/2 or 2;
- that the hold counts from when the estimates first agree, so a lasting move to, say, 3/4 time is followed some seconds after it happens, a short related passage doesn't move the lights, and unrelated changes are followed straight away.

**Logging paragraph (about line 185).** Add the two new INFO lines: one when the kick moves the tempo, and one when the tracker follows a related tempo after the hold.

**Test summary paragraph (about line 187).** Add the new tests:
- accents at related tempos, with the kick's tempo still winning;
- a steady tempo with no hops;
- a kick on every other beat;
- a lasting switch to a related tempo, followed after the hold;
- a short related passage, ignored;
- 100 to 128 BPM, followed as unrelated.

**Known limitations (about line 387).** Reword the "related but wrong tempo" item to say what the tracker still gets wrong: songs where the kick itself supports both tempos, and half or double time. Remove the "one of six songs recorded through BlackHole" sentence. Leave the "double or half time" item (line 386) as it is.
